{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"1d9d8187c08e1fd7","name":"card_event_escaut_plan","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/events/card_event_escaut_plan","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ESCAUT PLAN","text":"Target unit moves into the frontline, if possible. Give it Ambush, if this is the first order this turn.","flavorText":"The Escaut Plan was an operation planned by the French Army as a response if Germany invaded Belgium. It was an alternative to the Dyle Plan, in case Belgium didn’t allow the French troops to enter its territory quickly enough. It was adopted in October 1939 but never put into action. Motivated by military, economic and political reasons for the French and the British, both those plans aimed at stopping the German offensive in Belgium rather than on the French border. The Escaut Plan’s objective was to set up, in coordination with the Belgian Army, a defensive line along the Scheldt river (named Escaut in French), a river crossing Belgium from North to South, to defend the western part of the country. For that purpose, the fastest Allied troops were gathered in northern France: the British Expeditionary Force (partially motorized), and the French Light Mechanized Divisions (armored), Cavalry Divisions (part on horseback and part motorized) and Motorized Infantry Divisions. This plan was updated in November 1939 in order to also plan an intervention in the South of Netherlands, following intel collected by the Allies indicating the Germans intended to invade the country. When the German forces crossed the Belgian and Dutch borders on May 10th, 1940, the Belgian and Dutch governments immediately called the French for help, and the Dyle Plan was therefore launched.","faction":"France","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_escaut_plan","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_escaut_plan_title","SourceString":"ESCAUT PLAN","LocalizedString":"ESCAUT PLAN"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_escaut_plan_text","SourceString":"Target unit moves into the frontline, if possible. Give it Ambush, if this is the first order this turn.","LocalizedString":"Target unit moves into the frontline, if possible. Give it Ambush, if this is the first order this turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_escaut_plan_history","SourceString":"The Escaut Plan was an operation planned by the French Army as a response if Germany invaded Belgium. It was an alternative to the Dyle Plan, in case Belgium didn’t allow the French troops to enter its territory quickly enough. It was adopted in October 1939 but never put into action. Motivated by military, economic and political reasons for the French and the British, both those plans aimed at stopping the German offensive in Belgium rather than on the French border. The Escaut Plan’s objective was to set up, in coordination with the Belgian Army, a defensive line along the Scheldt river (named Escaut in French), a river crossing Belgium from North to South, to defend the western part of the country. For that purpose, the fastest Allied troops were gathered in northern France: the British Expeditionary Force (partially motorized), and the French Light Mechanized Divisions (armored), Cavalry Divisions (part on horseback and part motorized) and Motorized Infantry Divisions. This plan was updated in November 1939 in order to also plan an intervention in the South of Netherlands, following intel collected by the Allies indicating the Germans intended to invade the country. When the German forces crossed the Belgian and Dutch borders on May 10th, 1940, the Belgian and Dutch governments immediately called the French for help, and the Dyle Plan was therefore launched.","LocalizedString":"The Escaut Plan was an operation planned by the French Army as a response if Germany invaded Belgium. It was an alternative to the Dyle Plan, in case Belgium didn’t allow the French troops to enter its territory quickly enough. It was adopted in October 1939 but never put into action. Motivated by military, economic and political reasons for the French and the British, both those plans aimed at stopping the German offensive in Belgium rather than on the French border. The Escaut Plan’s objective was to set up, in coordination with the Belgian Army, a defensive line along the Scheldt river (named Escaut in French), a river crossing Belgium from North to South, to defend the western part of the country. For that purpose, the fastest Allied troops were gathered in northern France: the British Expeditionary Force (partially motorized), and the French Light Mechanized Divisions (armored), Cavalry Divisions (part on horseback and part motorized) and Motorized Infantry Divisions. This plan was updated in November 1939 in order to also plan an intervention in the South of Netherlands, following intel collected by the Allies indicating the Germans intended to invade the country. When the German forces crossed the Belgian and Dutch borders on May 10th, 1940, the Belgian and Dutch governments immediately called the French for help, and the Dyle Plan was therefore launched."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSuppressed"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/France/Mini_Ally_Expansion_25/t_escaut_plan.t_escaut_plan","SubPathString":""},"artist":"French WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/ESCAUT_PLAN.ESCAUT_PLAN","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":392.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_event_escaut_plan_photo","SourceString":"Soldiers of the British Expeditionary Force, Herseaux, Belgium, May 1940.","LocalizedString":"Soldiers of the British Expeditionary Force, Herseaux, Belgium, May 1940."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[{"name":"otherOrderPlayed","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"playedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"affectedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"orderPlayed","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_escaut_plan_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_GetOppositeSide_oppositeSide","type":"ESideEnum","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetOppositeSide_oppositeSide_1","type":"ESideEnum","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_DoesSideControlTheFrontline_doesHe","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_DoesSideControlTheFrontline_doesHe_1","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsLocationFull_isFull","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsUnit_isIt","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsUnit_isIt_1","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_EqualEqual_ByteByte_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in